**Issue**: #411
**Date**: 2026-09-22
**Status**: Approved
**Author**: NMG
**Related Spec**: specs/374-recover-bounded-automatic-delivery-stops-without-loops/

Feature: Recover issue-unreadable failed START after credentials return
  An original START failure may be retried once only when its evidence and restored issue access are proven.

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Credentials restored without mutation
    Given an exact clean original branch and HEAD with no START branch mutation or live worker
    And the current run has a valid failed intervention START handoff with reason issue_unreadable
    When a fresh read of that issue succeeds after prior credential failure
    Then discovery reports a bounded issue_unreadable_start_resume without changing evidence

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Consume exactly one ordinary START redispatch
    Given the original START failure remains exact under the controller lease
    When parameter-free execute resumes
    Then the failed handoff is archived byte-for-byte and a run-bound invocation is durably consumed
    And the normal START worker is dispatched once without any fabricated passed handoff

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Unsafe or stale proof cannot dispatch
    Given the handoff is malformed or changed, the issue read fails, branch or HEAD moves, the tree is dirty, a START branch exists, another worker or foreign lock is present, or the run identity differs
    When discovery or execute evaluates the retry
    Then it remains blocked without another worker or substituted success evidence

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Failed redispatch stays consumed
    Given a consumed START retry writes another failed handoff
    When recovery discovery runs again
    Then it remains blocked and preserves the original archive and invocation identity

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Unrelated recovery remains unchanged
    Given a different failed step or a passed START handoff
    When recovery is considered
    Then existing recovery and settlement behavior remains unchanged
